  "id": "Compound::DB06713 - Gene::5241",
  "verbalization": "Norelgestromin is closely related to progestin and steroid compounds through its inclusion in the Progesterone Congeners class, which includes Megestrol Acetate, Norgestimate, and Ethynodiol. These compounds all bind to the Pgr receptor, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving progestin receptor activation. The lowest common ancestors of Norelgestromin and its included compounds point to progestin and steroid pathways, reinforcing the notion that Norelgestromin interacts with Pgr through a progestin-like mechanism. The consistent evidence across the three paths indicates that Norelgestromin may act as a progestin analog, binding to the Pgr receptor and modulating its activity. This relationship is supported by the structural and functional similarities among the compounds, highlighting a potential role for Norelgestromin in progestin-related pathways.",
